<title>USA: ADR REPORT - LVMH rises in New York.</title>
<headline>ADR REPORT - LVMH rises in New York.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>French luxury goods group LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton rose on Friday in otherwise quiet post-holiday trade in American Depositary Receipts (ADRs).</p>
<p>&quot;We're seeing a thin (overall) market and we're just following along in suit,&quot; said an ADR trader.</p>
<p>LVMH rose 1-3/8 to 50-3/8, partly fueled by a report it may sell its 20 percent state in Guinness Plc and by its purchase of the prestigious Sauternes winemaker.  </p>
<p>Britain's Barclays Plc rose 1-1/2 to 69-7/8 amid renewed hopes for another share buyback. SmithKline Beecham Plc fell 1/4 to 45-5/8 amid speculation Roche Holding would bid for the company or try to merge with it.</p>
<p>Latin American bellwether Telebras, Brazil's telephone company, rose 1-5/8 to 75-1/2 following a recent rise in Sao Paulo. The stock &quot;is just trying to find a home in New York,&quot; one trader said.  </p>
<p>Advancers led decliners by a margin of 268 to 211 among 807 ADRs. Volume was low at 26.9 million shares.</p>
<p>-- Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879</p>
